<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lațcu of Moldavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1375</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lațcu was prince of Moldavia from about 1367 to about 1375, the son of Bogdan I. He sought a Catholic bishopric at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siret">Siret</a>, established around 1371, to win papal support against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. He was succeeded by Petru I Mușat, who did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1387.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/latcu-of-moldavia.jpg" alt="Lațcu of Moldavia" width="320" height="489" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Moldova · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_of_Moldova_196.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
